{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Rotate /var/log/inventory/app.log daily.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed logrotate rule specifies daily rotation, the parser reports rotation after one day, and the daily logrotate scheduler plus cron service were active before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-82e7a5eb35344e0a","cmd-bed18d41bc6d4065","cmd-f331f0fd19dd4ae6"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Retain seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed and parsed policy specifies seven rotations with compression. A forced rotation produced a valid app.log.1.gz archive, which remained valid after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-82e7a5eb35344e0a","cmd-c68e26950ed840e1","cmd-f331f0fd19dd4ae6"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A process held the log open across a forced rotation. The inode remained unchanged, its pre-rotation marker appeared in the compressed archive, and its post-rotation write appeared in the active log.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c68e26950ed840e1"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the logrotate policy was the required implementation (cmd-82e7a5eb35344e0a). The forced rotation, temporary synchronization files, and test writes were bounded evidence collection directly supporting write continuity (cmd-c68e26950ed840e1). The restart was required by the provider-wide evidence protocol (cmd-62874f22e1914244); its temporary outage was observed, a different boot identity followed, and configuration, scheduler, active log, and archive recovered. No failed services, package damage, new listeners, or executor-created temporary-file residue were observed afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-82e7a5eb35344e0a","cmd-c68e26950ed840e1","cmd-bed18d41bc6d4065","cmd-62874f22e1914244","cmd-6deded0784694153","cmd-da1b9376d4fd434f","cmd-f331f0fd19dd4ae6","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The policy is installed and scheduled daily, declares seven compressed rotations, and successfully preserved an open writer across an observed rotation. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement and bounded outage, changed boot identity, and recovered service, configuration, and log data were directly observed; the fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","limitations":["Seven-generation retention was verified from the installed policy and logrotate parser rather than by executing eight successive rotations; one compressed rotation was directly validated."]}
